   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The graph of the continuous function f shown consists of four line segments and a semicircle, for \\( 0 \\le x \\le 8 \\). Find \\( \\int_{2}^{8} f(x)\\,dx \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Add",
         [
            "Rational",
            -1,
            2
         ],
         [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "Pi"
         ]
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Between x = 2 and x = 4 the graph is made of line segments, so each unit strip is a trapezoid or a pair of triangles with signed area \\( \\frac{1}{2}, -1 \\), totalling \\( - \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -1,
            2
         ],
         "rule_named": "area of a trapezoid, negative below the axis"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "On [4, 8] the semicircle has radius 2, so its area is \\( \\tfrac{1}{2}\\pi (2)^2 = 2\\pi \\), counted as \\( 2 \\pi \\) because it lies above the axis.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "Pi"
         ],
         "rule_named": "area of a semicircle"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Adding the signed pieces gives \\( \\int_{2}^{8} f(x)\\,dx = - \\frac{1}{2} + 2 \\pi \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Rational",
               -1,
               2
            ],
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               "Pi"
            ]
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99069",
         "rule_named": "additivity over adjacent intervals"
      }
   ],
